Z||000000||contra||07-10-2000||08:11 AM||||I've almost got my car ship shape except for the cracked manifold, so i've started to customize. I got myself an IMSA style front lowering spoiler which i put on in 30mins yesterday and it looks amazing. It was kind of tough putting it on because the mold wasn't perfectly shaped to the fascia. I'm hoping that after it sits screwed on to the front it will cure to the shape with the hot summer heat. I'm going to put in some body filler along the seam between the fascia and the spoiler so that it looks like it's actually part of the car. But otherwise, i love the look. it makes it look like a nascar or something  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>My next challenge is my quarter panel scoops. Right now they're sanded and primed and ready to go on, i just have to get a free day or weekend to disassemble my rocker panels and crap. If anybody has any tips on removing quarter panels tell me now before i start.<P>Oh, also i got myself a pair of carbon fiber look wipers, and that vinyl carbon fiber dash kit stuff. Finished all that and it looks nice, i just need to do some more trimming. I'll post pictures as soon as i can find my digital camera.<P>||||reg||6
